(Department of Computer Science & Engineering - Semester 4) Tj
T*
T*
(UNIT 1: DATA STRUCTURES AND ALGORITHM ANALYSIS) Tj
T*
(----------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(1. Asymptotic Notations:) Tj
T*
(   - Big-O \(O\): Represents the upper bound of algorithm runtime \(Worst Case\).) Tj
T*
(   - Omega: Represents the lower bound of runtime \(Best Case\).) Tj
T*
(   - Theta: Represents the tight bound where upper and lower bounds meet.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Binary Search Trees \(BST\):) Tj
T*
(   - A binary tree where the left subtree contains keys smaller than the node.) Tj
T*
(   - The right subtree contains keys strictly greater than the root node.) Tj
T*
(   - Search, insertion, and deletion complexity: O\(h\) where h is tree height.) Tj
T*
(   - In a balanced BST \(AVL or Red-Black\), h = O\(log n\).) Tj
T*
(   - In a degenerate BST, worst-case complexity degrades to O\(n\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Common College Exam Questions:) Tj
T*
(   - Question: Differentiate between Stack \(LIFO\) and Queue \(FIFO\).) Tj
T*
(   - Question: Explain In-order, Pre-order, and Post-order tree traversals.) Tj
T*
ET
