(UNIT 2: DATABASE MANAGEMENT SYSTEMS \(DBMS\)) Tj
T*
(----------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(1. ACID Properties in Transaction Processing:) Tj
T*
(   - Atomicity: All operations succeed or none are applied \(All-or-Nothing\).) Tj
T*
(   - Consistency: Database moves from one valid state to another valid state.) Tj
T*
(   - Isolation: Concurrent transactions do not interfere with each other.) Tj
T*
(   - Durability: Committed changes survive power loss or system crash.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Database Normalization:) Tj
T*
(   - 1NF: Eliminates repeating groups; ensures atomic/indivisible values.) Tj
T*
(   - 2NF: In 1NF and removes partial functional dependencies on candidate keys.) Tj
T*
(   - 3NF: In 2NF and removes transitive functional dependencies \(X -> Y -> Z\).) Tj
T*
(   - BCNF: Stricter version of 3NF; for every X -> Y, X must be a super key.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Important Exam Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Candidate Keys formula: Minimal super key with uniqueness property.) Tj
T*
ET
